# Seed Code Mail — frontend (Vite) environment
#
# Copy to `frontend/.env` for local development and set the same variables in
# the Vercel project (Settings → Environment Variables) for Production,
# Preview and Development.
#
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ reach the browser bundle, and everything
# here is PUBLIC by design:
#
#   * the Supabase project URL and publishable (anon) key are meant to be
#     shipped to clients — access control is enforced by Row Level Security.
#
# NEVER put a value here that must stay secret: a Supabase service-role key, a
# Google OAuth client secret, the Gmail token encryption key, or a Gmail App
# Password. Vite inlines VITE_ values into the public JavaScript bundle. Those
# secrets belong to the Vercel server functions (`api/`) and to the send worker's
# own environment — see the root .env.example.

# --- Supabase (Data API + Auth) --------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://jptukeybgvuehdzghxfj.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Campaign send worker --------------------------------------------------
# URL of the campaign send worker service (README → "Campaign execution and the
# send worker"). This is used only for *campaign* delivery and for the worker
# status shown in Settings; reading the Inbox and sending ordinary email go
# through the app's own /api/gmail endpoints and never touch the worker.
#
#   PRODUCTION: the deployed worker service URL, e.g.
#               https://seedmail-worker.onrender.com
#   LOCAL DEV:  leave this BLANK to use http://127.0.0.1:8765 automatically,
#               or set it to that value explicitly.
#
# Do NOT set a localhost value in the Vercel project environment variables. A
# deployed site cannot reach your computer, and the app will refuse to use the
# value and report it as a configuration problem. The default below is blank for
# that reason; uncomment it only for local development.
# VITE_MAIL_WORKER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8765
VITE_MAIL_WORKER_URL=

# --- Gmail API backend -----------------------------------------------------
# Nothing to configure for a normal deployment: the Gmail endpoints live under
# /api/gmail on the SAME origin as the site, and the browser never holds a
# Google credential. Only set VITE_API_BASE_URL if you deliberately host those
# functions somewhere other than this site's origin.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://example.vercel.app

# --- Public site origin ----------------------------------------------------
# Used for canonical URLs and structured data. Production is HTTPS-only (an
# http:// request is answered with a 308 redirect to https://).
VITE_SITE_URL=https://mrseedmail.vercel.app
